[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:125. Tea for Two]
[00:00.760]Lesson 125. | 第125课。
[00:03.905]Can't you come in and have tea now, Peter? | 彼得，你现在不能进来喝茶吗？
[00:08.105]Not yet, dear. | 还没呢，亲爱的。
[00:09.800]I must water the garden first. | 我必须先给花园浇水。
[00:13.570]Do you have to water it now? | 你现在非得浇水吗？
[00:17.045]I'm afraid I must. | 恐怕我非浇不可。
[00:19.225]Look at it. | 看看它。
[00:20.630]It's terribly dry. | 太干了。
[00:23.330]What a nuisance! | 真讨厌！
[00:26.205]Last summer it was very dry too. | 去年夏天也很干。
[00:29.305]Don't you remember? | 你不记得了吗？
[00:31.085]I had to water it every day. | 我每天都得浇水。
[00:34.135]Well, I'll have tea by myself. | 嗯，那我只好自己喝茶了。
[00:38.275]That was quick. | 真快。
[00:41.065]Have you finished already? | 你已经完工了吗？
[00:43.235]Yes, dear. | 是的，亲爱的。
[00:44.825]Look out of the window. | 看看窗外。
[00:47.520]Good heavens! | 天哪！
[00:49.995]It's raining. | 下雨了。
[00:51.645]That means you needn't water the garden. | 那意味着你不必给花园浇水了。
[00:54.925]That was a pleasant surprise. | 这真是一个惊喜。
[00:57.680]It means I can have tea instead. | 这意味着我可以去喝茶了。